-- title:
--   ℤ-independent Hecke operators stay independent over ℂ
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number and let $S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ denote the space `CuspForm (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 N) 2` of weight-$2$ cusp forms for $\Gamma_0(N)$, viewed as a complex vector space. Inside the endomorphism algebra $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}} S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ consider the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 ∅`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), namely the $\mathbb{Z}$-algebra generated by the set of operators consisting of [`CuspForm.heckeTLin 2 hℓ hℓN`](def/ModularForm_HeckeOperatorForms.html#L69) for every prime $\ell$ not dividing $N$ together with [`CuspForm.heckeULin 2 hqN`](def/ModularForm_HeckeOperatorForms.html#L83) for every prime $q$ dividing $N$ (the exclusion set being empty, no generator is omitted). Let $\iota$ be a type and $T : \iota \to$ [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 ∅`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) a family of elements of this subalgebra which is linearly independent over $\mathbb{Z}$. The conclusion is that the family obtained by mapping each $T_i$ to its underlying element of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}} S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ is linearly independent over $\mathbb{C}$.
--
--   This is the rationality content of the Eichler–Shimura integral structure on the Hecke algebra: it says that the integral Hecke algebra of weight-$2$ cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ sits in its complex span as a lattice, so that its $\mathbb{Z}$-rank equals the dimension of that span, rather than merely dominating it. It is used in the construction of the integral structure [`CuspForm.hasIntegralStructure_two`](thm.html#CuspForm.hasIntegralStructure_two), which underlies the later passage from cusp forms to Galois representations.
-- source:
